Barehand Proficiency represents your training in unarmed combat. While
anyone can throw a punch, true proficiency requires learning proper
striking techniques, defensive postures, and how to generate power
without a weapon.

Higher proficiency increases your accuracy and effectiveness when fighting
without weapons. You learn to use your entire body as a weapon - fists,
elbows, knees, and feet all become tools of combat.

For most characters, barehand proficiency provides only basic competence
(dealing 1-3 damage). However, monks who combine this with their specialized
techniques such as Kubo can transform unarmed combat into a devastating
fighting style that rivals or exceeds armed combat.

Once you have achieved sufficient proficiency, monks may pursue Barehand
Specialization for additional attacks per round.

